-- je21-nouns: the nouns of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021), written once.
-- This module holds DECLARE and nothing else: no rule, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT.
-- Every other je21- module imports it.
-- The membership test for a noun here is: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this fact, or does answering it require reading the Law?
-- Only the first kind is here.
-- Whether an instrument "has been made", "is in force" or "is an official version" is a rule and lives with the Article that says so.
--
-- The seat is the reader of an enactment: someone who has to know what an enactment means for them, when it bound them,
-- what it lets be done to them, whether a notice reached them in time.
-- The facts in this module are facts that person could state.
--
-- Copying note.
-- je21-art03-commencement.l4 is meant to be COPIED by hand into another encoding (the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014's).
-- It imports only prelude, daydate and this module, so the nouns it needs are copied with it.
-- They are, in this order: `Time of day`, `Kind of legislation for Article 3(1)`, `Moment of coming into force`,
-- and the three reading enumerations L1, L2 and L3 (sections 1 and 3 below).
-- Everything else here is used by modules that are not copied.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. Time and the text of the Law (Articles 3 and 26; the forks L1 to L3)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A time of day on a day, in whole minutes.
-- The Law never states a time zone; none is carried here, and a caller who has a time must give it in the time kept in Jersey on that day.
DECLARE `Time of day` HAS
    `hour of the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The hour, 0 to 23, on a 24-hour clock
    `minute of the hour` IS A NUMBER @desc The minute, 0 to 59

-- Which text of the Law governs a day (endnotes: Table of Legislation History, and endnote [2]).
-- The Law came into force on 28 September 2021.
-- Two point-in-time versions are deposited: 28 September 2021 to 10 January 2024, and 11 January 2024 onwards.
DECLARE `Text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021` IS ONE OF
    `the Law was not in force`
    `the text of 28 September 2021`
    `the text of 11 January 2024`

-- The answer to any question dated before the Law came into force: a value, not a refusal.
DECLARE `Before the Law was in force` IS ONE OF
    `the Law was not in force on that date` HAS commencement IS A STRING @desc The commencement of the Law, as the endnotes give it

-- L1: Article 3(1)(b) says a silent provision comes into force "on the day after it is made".
-- Article 3(2) gives a beginning-of-day rule only for legislation "expressed to come into force on a particular day", and a silent provision is not expressed.
DECLARE `Reading L1 of the day after a silent provision is made` IS ONE OF
    `the Law does not say at what time of that day, so a question about a time of day on it is refused`
    `the provision is in force from the beginning of that day`

-- L2: Article 3(2) says a provision expressed to come into force on a particular day is treated as coming into force at the beginning of that day,
-- "unless provision is made to the contrary".
-- Whether a stated time of day is such a provision, the Law does not say.
DECLARE `Reading L2 of a stated time of day` IS ONE OF
    `a stated time of day is provision to the contrary, and the legislation comes into force at that time`
    `a stated time of day does not displace the beginning of the day`

-- L3: the time at which the Law came into force on 28 September 2021.
-- Articles 3(6) and 11(4) speak of the commencement of Part 2 and Articles 13(1) and 16(1)(a) of the commencement of Part 3; the endnotes record one commencement day for the whole Law.
-- The endnotes give the day, and R&O.112/2021 itself, which could state a time, is not among the sources.
-- Article 3(2) would put it at the beginning of the day.
DECLARE `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force` IS ONE OF
    `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)`
    `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 2. Kinds of legislation (Articles 1, 2, 7, 9 and 11)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The forms the Law names: Laws (Article 1 "Law"), Regulations including Triennial Regulations, Acts of the States, Orders, other instruments
-- (Article 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation"), and UK extended legislation (Article 1).
DECLARE `Form of legislation` IS ONE OF
    `a Law`
    `Regulations`
    `Triennial Regulations`
    `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation`
    `an Order`
    `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey`
    `UK extended legislation`

-- What Jersey subordinate legislation is made under (Article 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (a) and (b)).
DECLARE `What an instrument is made under` IS ONE OF
    `Jersey legislation`
    `UK extended legislation or an Order in Council registered in the Royal Court`
    `neither of these`

-- The facts that Article 1 turns on when it says what an instrument is.
DECLARE `Facts about an instrument` HAS
    `it is Regulations, an Order or another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument is Regulations, an Order or some other instrument that has legislative effect in Jersey
    `it was made in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument was made in Jersey
    `it is made under` IS A `What an instrument is made under` @desc What the instrument draws its power from
    `it was adopted by the States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument was adopted by the States
    `it relies on other legislation to empower its making` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if some other legislation gives the power to make it
    `it is a provision of a UK Act, or subordinate legislation made under a UK Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument is a provision of an Act of the Parliament of the United Kingdom, or subordinate legislation made under one
    `it has been registered in the Royal Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the instrument has been registered in the Royal Court

-- Article 1 "repeal": the words the definition names.
DECLARE `Word used for ending legislation` IS ONE OF
    `the word repeal`
    `the word delete`
    `the word rescind`
    `the word revoke`
    `another word`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 3. Making (Article 2; the forks L4 and L8)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- L4: Article 2(4) says Jersey legislation "has been made once it has been registered, adopted or signed as the case may be",
-- and for a Law Article 2(1) lists three steps, joined by "and".
-- The day on which a Law was made, when the three steps fall on different days, is not stated.
DECLARE `Reading L4 of the day on which a Law was made` IS ONE OF
    `the day it was registered, by Article 2(4)`
    `the latest of the days on which the three steps of Article 2(1) were done`

-- L8: Article 2(2) treats a taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 as made as a Law
-- "even though it has not yet completed the steps referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and (c)".
-- It says nothing about step (a), adoption by the States Assembly, and Article 12(1) of the 2019 Law is not among the sources.
DECLARE `Reading L8 of Article 2(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the declaration by Act of the States is all that Article 2(2) requires`
    `the taxation draft must also have been adopted by the States Assembly, which Article 2(2) does not excuse`

-- The steps of Article 2(1) and the deeming of Article 2(2).
DECLARE `Steps toward making a Law` HAS
    `it was adopted by the States Assembly on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day the States Assembly adopted it; leave empty if it has not
    `it was sanctioned by Order in Council on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day it was sanctioned by Order in Council (before 11 January 2024, by order of Her Majesty in Council); leave empty if it has not been
    `it was registered in the Royal Court on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day it was registered in the Royal Court; leave empty if it has not been
    `it is a taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if it is a taxation draft that an Act of the States has declared to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019

-- The steps of Article 2(3).
DECLARE `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` HAS
    `its form` IS A `Form of legislation` @desc Regulations, Triennial Regulations or an Act of the States (made by adoption), or an Order or another instrument (made by signing)
    `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc For Regulations or an Act: the day the proposition containing them was adopted by the States Assembly; leave empty if it has not been
    `it was signed on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc For any other subordinate legislation: the day it was signed; leave empty if it has not been
    `it was signed by the person responsible for making it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person responsible for making it signed it
    `it was made by a body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation is made by a body rather than by one person
    `it was signed by a person acting in accordance with the procedural requirements of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if, for legislation made by a body, the signer acted in accordance with the body's procedural requirements

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 4. Commencement (Article 3)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Article 3(1): the two cases of silence.
DECLARE `Kind of legislation for Article 3(1)` IS ONE OF
    `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation`
    `an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)`
    `any other legislation`

-- When a provision comes into force, as far as Article 3 says it.
-- The moment is a day and what the Law says about the time of day on it.
DECLARE `Moment of coming into force` IS ONE OF
    `from the beginning of the day` HAS day IS A DATE
    `from a stated time on the day` HAS day IS A DATE, time IS A `Time of day`
    `from the time it was made on the day` HAS day IS A DATE, `time of making` IS A MAYBE `Time of day`
    `at a time on the day that the Law does not state` HAS day IS A DATE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 5. Powers and repeal (Articles 4 to 10; the forks L5 and L6)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Article 4(1)(a) to (f).
DECLARE `Kind of power in Article 4(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation`
    `a power to establish an entity`
    `a power to make an appointment`
    `a power to give a notice or document`
    `a power to prescribe a form`
    `a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation`
    `a power of none of these kinds`

-- How legislation can come to an end for the purposes of Article 5 (5).
DECLARE `How legislation ended` IS ONE OF
    `it was repealed`
    `it expired`
    `it otherwise ceased to have effect`
    `it has not ended`

-- L9: Article 5(1) applies "where any Jersey legislation repeals any other Jersey legislation", and Article 5(5) says a reference to legislation being repealed
-- "includes a reference to its having expired or otherwise ceasing to have effect".
-- The heading is "Effect of repeal and expiry".
-- Whether legislation that expires with no other legislation repealing it is within paragraph (1), the words leave open.
DECLARE `Reading L9 of Article 5 and legislation that expires` IS ONE OF
    `Article 5 applies to legislation that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect, whether or not other legislation repealed it`
    `Article 5 applies only where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation`

-- L10: Article 5(2) and (4) begin "Unless provision is made to the contrary"; Article 5(3) does not.
-- Whether a contrary provision that displaces paragraph (2) displaces paragraph (3) too, the words leave open.
DECLARE `Reading L10 of Article 5(3) where provision is made to the contrary` IS ONE OF
    `a contrary provision that displaces paragraph (2) displaces paragraph (3) too, which speaks only of things mentioned in paragraph (2)`
    `paragraph (3) has no "unless" limb and applies even where paragraph (2) is displaced`

-- Article 5(2)(a) to (f): what a repeal does not affect, by default.
DECLARE `Thing a repeal might affect` IS ONE OF
    `the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered under the repealed legislation`
    `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it`
    `an amendment of legislation made by the repealed legislation`
    `the previous operation of the repealed legislation, or anything done or permitted under it`
    `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy that relates to a right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability under it`
    `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence committed, or a breach, before the repeal`

-- Article 5(4)(a) to (c): what a repeal does not revive, by default.
DECLARE `Thing a repeal might revive` IS ONE OF
    `legislation that was repealed`
    `a rule of law that had been abolished`
    `any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect`

-- L5: Articles 7(2), 9(6)(b) and 11(3) speak of legislation "not made by the States" and the Law does not say what that is.
DECLARE `Reading L5 of legislation made by the States` IS ONE OF
    `made by the States means adopted by the States Assembly, as Article 2(1)(a) and 2(3)(a) put it, so it covers Laws, Regulations and Acts`
    `made by the States means a Law only`

-- L6: Article 9(6) says the incidental power of Article 9(5) "is limited ... to amending" certain legislation.
DECLARE `Reading L6 of the limits in Article 9(6)` IS ONE OF
    `the limits bear on provision that amends other legislation, and incidental provision of any other kind is not limited by them`
    `the power in Article 9(5) is limited to amendments of the permitted kind, and authorises incidental provision of no other kind`

-- The legislation that an incidental provision under Article 9(5) would amend.
DECLARE `Legislation to be amended` HAS
    `its form` IS A `Form of legislation` @desc The form of the legislation that would be amended
    `it is the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation to be amended is the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000
    `it is the legislation giving the power to make the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation to be amended is the legislation that gives the power to make the instrument doing the amending

-- What the incidental power of Article 9(5), limited by Article 9(6), does for a provision.
DECLARE `What the incidental power does` IS ONE OF
    `Article 9(5) authorises the provision`
    `Article 9(6) bars the provision`
    `Article 9(5) does not apply because provision is made to the contrary`

-- Article 10(2): the facts about a document.
DECLARE `Facts about a document` HAS
    `it is legislation from some jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the document is legislation from any jurisdiction
    `it is accessible to the public without charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the public can get at the document without charge
    `it is concerned with the practices, procedures, processes or requirements for use of a technical product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the document is concerned with the practices, procedures, processes or requirements for use of a technical product
    `it is aimed at a person with particular knowledge or experience in that technical field` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the document is aimed at a person with particular knowledge or experience in that technical field

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 6. Annulment (Article 11; the fork L7)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- L7: Article 11(4) speaks of "the reference in paragraph (1) to 3 sittings after it is made", and paragraph (1) has no such reference:
-- it says "3 sittings after the date on which it is laid".
DECLARE `Reading L7 of Article 11(4)` IS ONE OF
    `the 3 sittings run from the commencement of Part 2, which is what paragraph (4) says`
    `paragraph (4) has no reference to apply to, so the 3 sittings run from the date of laying, as paragraph (1) says`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 7. Consolidation, revision, publication and official versions (Part 3)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Article 12.
DECLARE `Kind of text under Part 3` IS ONE OF
    `as-enacted legislation`
    `consolidated legislation`
    `revised legislation`

-- Article 14(1)(a) to (e): the editorial changes the Principal Legislative Drafter may make to consolidated legislation.
DECLARE `Editorial change under Article 14(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the removal of a provision relating to its commencement`
    `the removal of a provision that amends or repeals other legislation`
    `the removal of another provision that the Principal Legislative Drafter considers spent or no longer operative`
    `the correction of typographical and clerical errors`
    `the correction of errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation`
    `the correction of errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering`
    `the correction of errors in, or arising out of, an amendment by other legislation`
    `the correction of any other errors of a similar nature`
    `changes in punctuation, and the relocation of conjunctives or disjunctives, to add or remove a provision in a list`

-- Article 13(1): the events that call for a consolidated version.
DECLARE `Event that calls for a consolidated version` IS ONE OF
    `the legislation is commenced`
    `the legislation is amended`
    `the legislation is revised`
    `none of these has happened`

-- Where a published version stands, for Article 14(6).
DECLARE `Published version for Article 14(6)` IS ONE OF
    `a published version of as-enacted legislation, with an error that occurred after it was made`
    `a published version of revised legislation, with an error that occurred after its revision`
    `any other published version or error`

-- L11: Article 17(2) says consolidated legislation that meets its conditions "is an official version"; it does not say "only if".
-- Article 1 says "official version" is construed in accordance with Article 17, and Article 17(6) lets the States vary the requirements of paragraph (2) by Regulations.
-- Whether a consolidated text that does not meet paragraph (2) is thereby not an official version, or the Law does not say, the words leave open.
DECLARE `Reading L11 of whether Article 17(2) is the only route to an official version of consolidated legislation` IS ONE OF
    `Article 17(2) is the only route, so consolidated legislation that does not meet it is not an official version`
    `Article 17(2) is a sufficient route, so whether other consolidated legislation is an official version is not answered`

-- The facts about a text that Article 17 turns on.
DECLARE `Facts about a text` HAS
    `its kind` IS A `Kind of text under Part 3` @desc As-enacted, consolidated or revised legislation
    `it is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the legislation is Jersey legislation, as opposed to UK extended legislation
    `it contains a statement that it is an official version of the legislation issued under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the text carries that statement
    `it is an electronic version displayed on a website under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter, or a printed or downloaded copy of that without any alteration to its text or format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the text is such an electronic version or an unaltered printed or downloaded copy
    `it is a printed version issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the text is a printed version issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter

-- Article 18(1) and (2): what Statute Law Revision Regulations may amend legislation for.
DECLARE `Ground of an amendment under Article 18` IS ONE OF
    `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation`
    `the amendment is necessary or desirable to reconcile inconsistencies between different provisions of the legislation, or between any of its provisions and provisions of any other Jersey legislation`
    `the amendment uses a power set out in Article 14`
    `the amendment uses a power set out in Schedule 1`
    `the amendment rests on none of these`

-- Schedule 1(a) to (q): the powers of the Law Revision Board in preparing a revision.
DECLARE `Power in Schedule 1` IS ONE OF
    `Schedule 1(a): to amend the citation provision, long title, short title, words of enactment or preamble`
    `Schedule 1(b): to consolidate or split legislation, or relocate a provision into different legislation`
    `Schedule 1(c): to rearrange the provisions of legislation, or a list in a provision`
    `Schedule 1(d): to add a table of contents or destinations`
    `Schedule 1(e): to add a heading to a provision that has none, or alter a heading`
    `Schedule 1(f): to omit any map, picture, drawing, diagram or other object`
    `Schedule 1(g): to change a reference to reflect a change of name, transfer of function or provision for construction`
    `Schedule 1(h): to make adaptations and amendments that appear necessary or proper as a consequence of constitutional or other changes`
    `Schedule 1(i): to change words to make them gender neutral`
    `Schedule 1(j): to change expressions of date, money, number, time and units of measurement`
    `Schedule 1(k): to delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions`
    `Schedule 1(l): to alter words to secure uniformity of expression`
    `Schedule 1(m): to shorten a phrase or sentence`
    `Schedule 1(n): to change the wording for the better application of plain language principles`
    `Schedule 1(o): to add numbering to, or renumber, a provision`
    `Schedule 1(p): to substitute a reference to legislation that has been re-enacted or replaced`
    `Schedule 1(q): to do all other things that appear to the Board to be necessary to render revised legislation consistent with current drafting practice`

-- The authority a draft revision relies on for one change (Article 15(6): "the power relied on as authority for the change").
DECLARE `Authority relied on for a change` IS ONE OF
    `a power in Schedule 1` HAS power IS A `Power in Schedule 1`
    `a power in Article 14` HAS `the change` IS AN `Editorial change under Article 14(1)`
    `no power is stated`

-- One change in a draft revision.
DECLARE `Change in a draft revision` HAS
    `what the change does` IS A STRING @desc A short description of the change
    `the authority relied on` IS AN `Authority relied on for a change` @desc The power in Article 14 or Schedule 1 that the statement accompanying the draft relies on for this change

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 8. The Legislative Drafting Office (Part 4)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Article 1 "Legislative Drafter".
DECLARE `Role in the Legislative Drafting Office` IS ONE OF
    `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office`
    `the Principal Legislative Drafter`
    `a trainee Legislative Drafter`
    `none of these`

-- Article 22(2) "provider of instructions".
DECLARE `Facts about a provider of instructions` HAS
    `is a Member of the States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person is a Member of the States
    `is an officer working in a department established by the States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person is an officer working in a department established by the States
    `is an officer working in a body, office or unit of administration established on behalf of the States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person is an officer working in a body, office or unit of administration established on behalf of the States, including under any legislation
    `otherwise provides instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person, though none of the above, gives instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office

-- Article 22(2) "confidential communications".
DECLARE `Kind of communication under Article 22` IS ONE OF
    `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office`
    `a communication between a client of the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter that relates to the subject matter of the instructions`
    `an unpublished draft of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the Legislative Drafting Office`
    `any other communication`
